            <ArticleTitle>Dataset on outdoor behavior-system and spatial-pattern in the third place in cold area-based on the perspective of new energy structure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>593-597</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dib.2016.12.040</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The data presented in this paper are related to the research article entitled &quot;Exploration of Outdoor Behavior System and Spatial Pattern in the Third Place in Cold Area- based on the perspective of new energy structure&quot; (Ren, 2016) [1]. The dataset was from a field sub-time extended investigation to residents of Power Home Community in Inner Mongolia of China that belongs to cold region of ID area according to Chinese design code for buildings. This filed data provided descriptive statistics about environment-behavior symbiosis system, environment loading, behavior system, spatial demanding and spatial pattern for all kinds of residents (Older, younger, children). The field data set is made publicly available to enable critical or extended analyzes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
